<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n39517" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπιίστωρ</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ορος</span>,
			ὁ, ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>privy to</i> a thing: c.gen.,
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μεγάλων ἔργων ἐ</span>. <i>privy
				to</i> great works (i.e. the robbery of the mares), <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				21.26
			</span></i>; so <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τεῶν μύθων ἐ</span>. <i><span class="en">
				A.R.
				4.89
			</span></i>: abs., ib.<i><span class="en">
				16
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>.
				<i>acquainted with, practised</i>
			<i>in</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δίσκων, γεωμετρίης</span>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				11.371
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Pall.
			</span></i>), <i><span class="en">
				<u>App.Anth.</u>
				7.2
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Euc.
			</span></i>); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σοφίης</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>IG</u>
					3.946
				</span></i>
			, cf. Doroth.in <i><span class="en">
				<u>Cat.Cod.Astr.</u>
				2.172
			</span></i>.</div>
